","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(m) to start. Each removal recomputes the betweenness of the removed edge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component C alone, O(n_C · m_C); every split builds a partition in O(n). The whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence is O(m² n) in the worst case.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/girvanNewmanCommunities()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Girvan–Newman communities: the successively finer partitions found by removing, again and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, the edge of greatest betweenness ("},{"code":"edgeBetweennessCentrality()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), recomputed after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each removal. A tie goes to the least edge position; parallel copies share their pairs’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths, and self-loops are never removed and never matter. The sequence is lazy: each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition is computed when iteration reaches it."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://CommunityDetection/documentation/CommunityDetection/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/CommunityDetection\/documentation\/CommunityDetection\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/communitydetection\